 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "transactions is a list of [timestamp, type, amount, price] string rows ordered by non-decreasing timestamp; type is \"buy\" or \"sell\"; amount and price are decimal integers. Shares are held in lots, one per buy, at the buy price. A sell of amount shares consumes held shares from the lots with the highest buy price first (the heap-greedy rule). The profit of a sell is the sum over consumed shares of (sell price - lot price); its tax is 10% of the profit when the profit is positive and 0 otherwise. Return the total tax as a decimal string with exactly one digit after the point (exact, since each tax is a whole number of tenths).",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk16-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
